{
  "comment": [
    "Golden vectors for tree sizes records (docs/scm.md, \"Tree sizes\").",
    "Both internal/scm/encoding (Go) and jj's encoding (Rust) must encode every valid record's",
    "sizes to exactly its bytes, decode those bytes back to the same sizes, and reject every invalid",
    "input with its error code. A byte string is the concatenation of its lines; each line is hex, and",
    "anything after '#' is a comment. Sizes are decimal strings: JSON numbers cannot hold every uint64."
  ],
